  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 705 PM EDT Thursday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Near normal temperatures and isolated to widely \nscattered afternoon/evening showers and storms are expected to \ncontinue through the weekend. \n\nThe latest wx analysis depicted high pressure centered off the \nMid- Atlantic/Southeast coast, with upper troughing in the \nPlains and Midwest. Temps as of 7 PM were generally in the upper\n80s with dew points in the mid 70s. A few isolate storms were\nnoted across the NW Piedmont moving into Spotsylvania County.\nThese storms are expected to move ENE, potentially crossing over\nfar northern portions of the FA early this evening. However,\nconfidence in these storms reaching the Eastern Shore is low at\nthis time. Another area of scattered showers and storms was\nnoted across central NC. This activity was generally lifting\nnorth and may move into portions of the southern Piedmont this\nevening. Otherwise, convection should decrease in coverage\novernight with showers and storms tapering off by around\nmidnight. Partly cloudy skies with lows in the 70s are expected\ntonight into Friday morning.\n\nSimilar conditions are expected Friday into the weekend (except that \ntemps may be a couple degrees warmer). A few locations near the \nVA/NC coast could see brief 105F heat indices each day, but not \nexpecting this to be enough to warrant an advisory. Still expect to \nsee some slight height falls over the local area as the upper ridge \noffshore retreats a bit to the SE and a series of weak shortwaves \npass by to our N/NW. This will lead to slightly greater chances for \ndiurnally driven showers or storms on Friday and Saturday across \nwestern and northern portions of the area but PoPs generally remain \naob 50%. A few storms are possible on Sunday, with the highest \nprecip chances (still only ~30%) shifting to SE VA/NE NC. It may be \neven hotter (with continued humid wx and minimal precip chances) on \nMon/Tue ahead of an approaching front. There is a low chc of Heat \nAdvisory conditions across SE portions of the FA early next\nweek.",
